window.EN={"1":"Following Hector's dying wish,","2":"Roy and his companions began advancing west, heading for the Ostia domain that Lilina was watching over in their absence.","3":"Along the way, they approached the Laus territory, governed by one of the Lycian lords, Erik.","4":"A land of plains blanketed everywhere, with a river carrying abundant water... In this peaceful land of Laus,","5":"Roy and his companions would come face to face with a dark conspiracy steadily advancing.","6":"Well, well, well — Lord Narcian.","7":"Lord Erik. Your submission to Bern is most welcome.","8":"If we remain bound by old pacts, there will be no future for us.","9":"Our future lies together with the Kingdom of Bern...","10":"That's a fine attitude to have. Kuh-huh-huh...","11":"By the way, where's that little gift of yours? She doesn't seem to be here.","12":"Oh, of course! She's already been prepared in another room.","13":"Heh heh heh... She's quite the naive, sheltered girl.","14":"I told her I'd let her see her brother, who's away on military duty, and she fell right into our hands, easy as that.","15":"Hey, bring her in!","16":"Where is this? Big brother... where's big brother Klein?","17":"Welcome, Lady Clarine.","18":"Who... who are you?","19":"I am Narcian, one of Bern's Three Dragon Generals.","20":"In your brother's place, I'll dote on you plenty myself.","21":"Kuh-huh-huh...","22":"...Hmph.","23":"? What's so funny, Lady Clarine?","24":"In my brother's place? You? Why don't you take a good look at yourself in a mirror.","25":"That outfit, that hairstyle, that way of speaking —","26":"Everything about you, from head to toe, is nothing but \"vulgar,\" isn't it?","27":"V-v-vulgar!? Me? Vulgar?","28":"Compared to my brother, you're like the moon next to a turtle!","29":"Damn you... I won't forgive this, I won't forgive this!!","30":"This little brat — of all things — calling me \"vulgar\"!!","31":"Lord Narcian, word has come that Castle Araphen has been retaken by the enemy!","32":"What!? What about Slater?","33":"Sir... his whereabouts are unknown.","34":"The enemy are remnants of the Lycian Alliance, and reports say their leader is Roy, the eldest son of House Pherae...","35":"......","36":"Tch! Lord Erik — throw this brat into the dungeon.","37":"When I get back, I'll have my fill of tormenting her!","38":"And close off the road to Ostia — those fools might pass through it.","39":"Yes, sir!!","40":"To think I'd be locked up in a place like this...","41":"...Hey.","42":"Who's there!?","43":"I'm a mercenary of this castle. Come out — Lord Erik has business with you.","44":"I don't want to! Why would I go with vulgar men like you...","45":"...Enough talk. Come out!","46":"Wait, let go of me! How rude! Do you know who I am...","47":"......","48":"I said let go of me!","49":"Let go of me! I said let go...","50":"Be quiet. You'll end up unable to escape.","51":"! You...","52":"There's a horse tied up by the trees just ahead.","53":"Ride it and get away, quickly.","54":"...Why? Why are you helping me?","55":"I have a grudge against Bern.","56":"A grudge?","57":"That's none of your concern.","58":"Being spoken to like that only makes me more curious.","59":"Time's running out. Go, quickly!","60":"......","61":"This is... the middle of a battlefield, isn't it!?","62":"...That swordsman! How inconsiderate of him!!","63":"Seeing a lady safely home is supposed to be a gentleman's \"proper manner\"!","64":"Whew... and all because I wanted to see my brother, who's off in the west...","65":"I snuck out of the mansion myself, and look how miserable this turned out...","66":"Whatever should I do...","67":"Heheheh...","68":"\"It's Lycia, it's Bern\" — must be rough being someone important.","69":"But for us, that just means it's all the more a good time to make some money.","70":"Oh, you've come! I've been waiting for you.","71":"...What do you need?","72":"Our forces outside are struggling. Take a few men and go help them.","73":"......","74":"Can't you hear me!? Go help them at once...","75":"I heard you. I'll go once I'm ready.","76":"Tch, what an unfriendly fellow... Well, he does seem skilled with a blade, at least.","77":"......","78":"Hey, excuse me — you there!","79":"Huh? Me?","80":"Who else would I be talking to? You're the leader of this army, aren't you?","81":"Yeah, that's right.","82":"How convenient. You — escort me.","83":"Huh?","84":"Didn't you hear me? I said escort me.","85":"What, what is this — listening quietly while this little brat...!!","86":"I wasn't talking to you. Stay out of this.","87":"Wh-what did you say!?","88":"Now, now, Marinus.","89":"It looked like she was being chased by the castle's men, so she probably wants us to protect her, right?","90":"W-well, that's... about the gist of it, yes.","91":"What!? What nerve, what shameless cheek!!","92":"Our army isn't soft enough to go keeping some useless little brat around!","93":"I'm Clarine! Would you kindly stop calling me \"little brat\"?","94":"And \"useless,\" you say — how rude of you!","95":"I can use a staff, so at the very least I could help an injured person...","96":"So you mean you'll fight alongside us?","97":"...O-of course I will.","98":"I-I'm not the type to just be protected for nothing...","99":"That's a relief!","100":"Against an enemy like Bern, the more fighting power we have, the better.","101":"I'm Roy. Nice to meet you, Clarine.","102":"Likewise, I...","103":"H-hmph! Don't think we're friends now.","104":"Ah! You're...","105":"What, you're still here?","106":"\"Still,\" you say!","107":"You dumped me in the middle of a battlefield, and you can say something like that!?","108":"If even one thing had gone wrong, I could have ended up in terrible trouble, you know!","109":"Lucky for you nothing did. Is that all you wanted to say?","110":"Wait a moment! You abandon me and just walk off like that, is that your plan?","111":"If you're going to act like a gentleman, you should properly take \"responsibility\" for it.","112":"\"Responsibility\"? What's that supposed to mean?","113":"Protecting a lady you've rescued and seeing her home is a gentleman's \"proper manner\" — in other words, his duty!","114":"I've never once heard of a story where the hero abandons the lady partway through, from any bard.","115":"...What in the world are you even talking about?","116":"In any case, didn't you have a grudge against Bern?","117":"And yet you turn your sword on us, who are fighting against Bern...","118":"Wait a moment! Is that true?","119":"Huh? What do you mean?","120":"Is this army opposing Bern!?","121":"Y-yes, that's what I heard from your leader, Roy.","122":"...Fine. Understood.","123":"Eh?","124":"I'll fight alongside you lot. That should settle things, shouldn't it?","125":"Y-yes, well...","126":"Honestly! What matters isn't \"fighting Bern\" — it's \"protecting me\"...","127":"Bandits and pirates sometimes attack villages, you know.","128":"A village that's been attacked gets destroyed, and nothing's left anymore.","129":"If only someone would go warn the village, they could be saved...","130":"Doors and treasure chests, you know — they won't open without a thief around.","131":"'Cause a thief's key can only be used by a thief, right?","132":"But get this — with THIS key, anyone can open any door, no matter what!","133":"I call it... the Door Key!","134":"You should be grateful — this is a seriously precious item, you know.","135":"Well, I guess... you can also just buy one at the item shop, though.","136":"Those mounted archers in the Laus army — those are the nomads.","137":"I hear those Sacae tribesfolk, and the Ilia knights up north too, make for capable mercenaries.","138":"In times like these, every country wants all the fighting strength it can get, I suppose.","139":"All of us here are on your side, you know.","140":"Abandoning the country you were born in and turning traitor to the enemy — that's something that should never be done.","141":"Take this treasured sword with you.","142":"This is a very valuable item, you know... Ah, don't touch it just yet.","143":"Look at this splendid shine — it takes your breath away, doesn't it.","144":"This was handed down to my great-great-great-grandfather by the king, a treasure with a proud history...","145":"You there — do you know the secret art of combat?","146":"The sword is strong against the axe, and the axe is strong against the lance.","147":"And then, the lance is strong against the sword.","148":"How about it? Before you sleep, you must chant this three times without fail...","149":"...What? You already knew that? Hmm... then how about this?","150":"I hear there are weapons out there that can reverse that very principle.","151":"Now what was it called...? I think it was something like the \"...buster\"...","152":"To think a war like this would actually break out...","153":"I wonder if this village too will end up placed under Bern's rule...","154":"If it's going to be taken by those Bernese soldiers anyway... I'd rather entrust it to you all.","155":"This is a magic robe that heightens the very wellspring of life.","156":"If you wear this, you should become someone who won't fall even from minor wounds.","157":"However... once used, even just once, it will be lost.","158":"Since it's such a precious item, please think it over carefully before using it.","159":"You fools, bound by moldy old pacts.","160":"Let me teach you the way of the world!","161":"Puhaha... how foolish.","162":"For those who defy the strong, there is no future either way...","163":"Lord Roy! The Laus soldiers' resistance has stopped.","164":"I see, understood. Let's take a short rest — go tell everyone.","165":"Yes, sir.","166":"Lord Roy... are you alright?","167":"...To think Lord Erik would betray us to Bern, of all things...","168":"I thought the Lycian Alliance was united, solid as a single slab of rock, but...","169":"Damn Bern, doing something so filthy!","170":"...I'm sorry.","171":"Ah... I'm sorry! I spoke without even considering Princess Guinivere's feelings.","172":"No... it's only natural that you would.","173":"From here, we're headed west, to Ostia.","174":"But now that Lord Hector has passed away, and the remaining lords can't be relied on either,","175":"the hope for peace... I'm afraid, may have already been severed.","176":"Princess, will you be returning to your own country? If there's anything we can help with...","177":"No — if it wouldn't trouble you, please let me come along too.","178":"It's no trouble at all... but why?","179":"...My brother is wrong.","180":"To revive dragons and drag them into a war among men...","181":"If that is what my brother calls \"liberating\" the world, then I want to stop it.","182":"\"Liberating\" the world?","183":"Yes — it's my brother's pet phrase. \"The world must be 'liberated'\"...","184":"And this war too, I believe, is for that very purpose...","185":"What does that even mean?","186":"Even I don't know that much...","187":"But my brother isn't the kind of person to simply think in terms of conquering the world.","188":"Surely there's some reason behind it, some reason I can't yet see.","189":"But even so, that doesn't make it right to start a war and take innocent lives...","190":"...Princess Guinivere."};
